.TH "rofimoji\-rofi" "7" "2026\-08\-29" "Version 6.8.0" "Rofi Third\-party Add\-on Documentation"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fBrofimoji\-rofi\fR \- Running \fBrofimoji\fR as a rofi mode
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBrofi\fR \fB\-modi\fR \fIemoji:rofimoji\fR \fB\-show\fR \fIemoji\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBrofimoji\fR can be integrated into \fBrofi\fR as a mode, so that it appears
alongside rofi'\&s other modes (applications, window list, etc.\&).\& This is
useful when \fBrofimoji\fR should behave as just another entry in a unified
launcher rather than as a standalone dialog.\&
.PP
Because \fBrofi\fR is the main process in this mode, \fBrofimoji\fR cannot
directly type characters into other windows.\& Only clipboard\-based
actions are available, so \fB\-\-action\fR should be set to \fIcopy\fR,
\fIclipboard\fR, \fIcopy\-unicode\fR, \fIprint\fR, or \fImenu\fR.\& The \fItype\fR,
\fItype\-numerical\fR, and \fIunicode\fR actions will not work.\&
.PP
Configuration options are otherwise the same as for the standalone
invocation; see \fBrofimoji\fR(1) for the full list.\&
.PP
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.PP
The same keybinding options as in standalone mode apply (see
\fBrofimoji\fR(1)), but rofi owns the keybinding table, so the shortcuts
are remapped to \fIAlt+Shift\fR combined with the configured keys.\& On a
Qwerty keyboard the defaults become:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fIEnter\fR: perform the default action
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+Shift+c\fR: copy the selected character to the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+Shift+p\fR: insert the selected character via the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+Shift+i\fR: copy the Unicode codepoint to the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+Shift+1\fR, \fIAlt+Shift+2\fR, .\&.\&.\&: insert the Nth\-most\-recently\-used
character
.PD
.PP
The \fIAlt+Shift+t\fR, \fIAlt+Shift+n\fR, and \fIAlt+Shift+u\fR keybindings (type,
type\-numerical, unicode) are mapped but have no effect, since \fBrofimoji\fR
cannot type in this mode.\&
.PP
Unlike standalone mode, multiple\-character selection via \fIShift+Enter\fR
is not available: only a single character can be selected at a time.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show the emoji mode:
.RS 4
$ rofi \-modi emoji:rofimoji \-show emoji
.RE
Combine the emoji mode with others in a \fIcombi\fR:
.RS 4
$ rofi \-modi combi \-show combi \-combi\-modi "window,drun,emoji:rofimoji"
.RE
